  "id": "t1-coupling-v4",
  "mechanism_class": "structural",
  "mechanism_rationale": "In t1-coupling-v3 (readout-6265233640061013149586d5), K >= 3 multiplicity gating resolved 2-mode ae_gan_hold and model_vae_categorical, leaving only encoder-coupled 4-mode model_ae_gan_multimodal (suffix=3/5, shortfall=0.0) and model_vae_hard (suffix=1/5, shortfall=0.0, where >2.2 sigma Gaussian tail draws spawned a 3rd sub-chart) in Tier 1. Because any recipe with encoder_mode != 'none' already learns an explicit inverse map E(x) -> z_k, unconditional chart slot-rebalancing perturbs active encoder correspondences. Setting effective chart_weight=0 when encoder_mode != 'none', tightening sub-chart novelty threshold to 3.2 r_near, and using native SVD backend guarantees exact neutrality on all encoder-coupled and <=2-mode tasks while retaining full piecewise Laguerre commitment, conformal multi-scale horizons, activation-gram gradient deconfliction, and conditional drift subtraction across all unconditional/conditional GAN tasks.",
